57 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(Firstly, writing a birth plan is NOT a silly idea or an invitation to be disappointed. Anyone who thinks that way is not yet informed about how bloody important a birth plan is! A birth plan is not a prescription or a set of instructions, its just a clear presentation of what you want! It will help your care providers to know exactly what you want without asking you a million questions but most importantly it will help YOU and your birth partner/s to learn all the options available and know what you want!)/E(Firstly, writing a birth plan is NOT a silly idea or an invitation to be disappointed. Anyone who thinks that way is not yet informed about how bloody important a birth plan is! A birth plan is not a prescription or a set of instructions, its just a clear presentation of what you want! It will help your care providers to know exactly what you want without asking you a million questions but most importantly it will help YOU and your birth partner/s to learn all the options available and know what you want!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

58 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(Visual Birth Plan Icons. You can find these on www.pinterandmartin.com. These are a great way to have a first look at what all the options are. There are likely to be lots of them that you hadn\220t considered or have just never heard of before. Find out what they all mean if you\220re not sure, knowing what all the options are is a great way to start figuring out what you would like to choose!)/E(Visual Birth Plan Icons. You can find these on www.pinterandmartin.com. These are a great way to have a first look at what all the options are. There are likely to be lots of them that you hadn\220t considered or have just never heard of before. Find out what they all mean if you\220re not sure, knowing what all the options are is a great way to start figuring out what you would like to choose!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

59 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(You are looking to create AT LEAST 3 birth plans. Think about what changes could happen. Eg. Home birth to hospital, spontaneous to induction etc. You would then create birth plans for each scenario with plan A being your ideal birth and plan C being a caesarean birth. Someone planning a Labour ward birth may do a plan A for that ideal birth they are working towards, a plan B for if they decide to have an induction or any augmentation \(waters being broken, the drip etc.\) and then a final plan C for caesarean. If plan A was a home birth or birth centre birth then there may be a plan B x2 for a change of birth place too!)/E(You are looking to create AT LEAST 3 birth plans. Think about what changes could happen. Eg. Home birth to hospital, spontaneous to induction etc. You would then create birth plans for each scenario with plan A being your ideal birth and plan C being a caesarean birth. Someone planning a Labour ward birth may do a plan A for that ideal birth they are working towards, a plan B for if they decide to have an induction or any augmentation \(waters being broken, the drip etc.\) and then a final plan C for caesarean. If plan A was a home birth or birth centre birth then there may be a plan B x2 for a change of birth place too!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

60 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(Think about what you want! What\220s important to you? What birth have you always thought would be lovely? At this point it doesn\220t matter what type of birth you think you are limited to, for now you are just getting an idea of the type of birth you would love to have. The next steps will help you find out how you can make this happen or what alternatives there are.)/E(Think about what you want! What\220s important to you? What birth have you always thought would be lovely? At this point it doesn\220t matter what type of birth you think you are limited to, for now you are just getting an idea of the type of birth you would love to have. The next steps will help you find out how you can make this happen or what alternatives there are.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

61 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(What special circumstances do you need to consider? Find out everything you can about these- Places like Evidence Based Birth, Sara Wickham\220s website, the NICE guidelines, AIMS. These may be health issues of your own, pregnancy related issues, health issues for baby. Not all of these will affect your birth choices but now is the time to find out which ones do if you have any!)/E(What special circumstances do you need to consider? Find out everything you can about these- Places like Evidence Based Birth, Sara Wickham\220s website, the NICE guidelines, AIMS. These may be health issues of your own, pregnancy related issues, health issues for baby. Not all of these will affect your birth choices but now is the time to find out which ones do if you have any!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

62 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 37 0 R/T(Find out others experiences. For example, If you would love a home birth and you have gestational diabetes, Join a FB group like Home Birth Support Group UK and look for others experiences with GD. This can be a great way of getting some insight into what other people have found useful when making their decisions and the different care provider opinions others have come across. This might show you that it\220s not as black and white as you may have been led to believe. No matter what it is always your choice.)/E(Find out others experiences. For example, If you would love a home birth and you have gestational diabetes, Join a FB group like Home Birth Support Group UK and look for others experiences with GD. This can be a great way of getting some insight into what other people have found useful when making their decisions and the different care provider opinions others have come across. This might show you that it\220s not as black and white as you may have been led to believe. No matter what it is always your choice.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

63 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Talk through your options with knowledgable folks. Leanne or the AIMS helpline would be a good start, they can tell you what they know, any relevant research and help you come up with a list of questions for you to ask your care providers as well as stuff to read up on.)/E(Talk through your options with knowledgable folks. Leanne or the AIMS helpline would be a good start, they can tell you what they know, any relevant research and help you come up with a list of questions for you to ask your care providers as well as stuff to read up on.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

64 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Discuss with your care provider. This may be a midwife or a consultant, do not be disheartened if you don\220t hear what you would like to hear, you can still chat through your circumstances with a Professional Midwifery Advocate and they can talk you through if what you are after is REALLY out of the question or not. \(note, it rarely is!\))/E(Discuss with your care provider. This may be a midwife or a consultant, do not be disheartened if you don\220t hear what you would like to hear, you can still chat through your circumstances with a Professional Midwifery Advocate and they can talk you through if what you are after is REALLY out of the question or not. \(note, it rarely is!\))/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

65 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Consider what things are super important to you and you would not like to miss out on unless theres an emergency. This may be remaining upright throughout labour and for the birth, skin to skin after birth, avoiding \217the drip\220 or any other intervention or medication etc. How can you try to make sure that you can have these things? Can they be worked into all your birth plans? Eg. Remaining upright- even in the case of epidural use you can be assisted into various positions that support birth. Skin to skin after birth, can it be arranged that your birth partner holds baby on your chest for skin to skin EVEN after a Caesarean under general anaesthetic? Avoiding \217the drip\220, this may mean you opt for a caesarean if you would rather. There are so many possibilities we\220re not always offered, if you aren\220t sure how you can still incorporate certain things then talk to your instructor!)/E(Consider what things are super important to you and you would not like to miss out on unless theres an emergency. This may be remaining upright throughout labour and for the birth, skin to skin after birth, avoiding \217the drip\220 or any other intervention or medication etc. How can you try to make sure that you can have these things? Can they be worked into all your birth plans? Eg. Remaining upright- even in the case of epidural use you can be assisted into various positions that support birth. Skin to skin after birth, can it be arranged that your birth partner holds baby on your chest for skin to skin EVEN after a Caesarean under general anaesthetic? Avoiding \217the drip\220, this may mean you opt for a caesarean if you would rather. There are so many possibilities we\220re not always offered, if you aren\220t sure how you can still incorporate certain things then talk to your instructor!)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

66 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Create the birth plans for real! Consider everything you\220ve learned about any factors concerning your pregnancy and chats with PMA or midwife etc and bring it all together to create your plan using whichever format suits you best, try to ensure it will be easily read by the care providers and explained by your birth partner. )/E(Create the birth plans for real! Consider everything you\220ve learned about any factors concerning your pregnancy and chats with PMA or midwife etc and bring it all together to create your plan using whichever format suits you best, try to ensure it will be easily read by the care providers and explained by your birth partner. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

67 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Create your plan methodically by first considering your background such as how you feel about birth, how many babies you\220ve had, any special medical or cultural requirements. )/E(Create your plan methodically by first considering your background such as how you feel about birth, how many babies you\220ve had, any special medical or cultural requirements. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

68 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Then move onto the things that you would like to include in your environment such as low light levels, quiet, who you would like present \(eg. Are you happy to have student midwives present? A doula?\). )/E(Then move onto the things that you would like to include in your environment such as low light levels, quiet, who you would like present \(eg. Are you happy to have student midwives present? A doula?\). )/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

69 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Next consider what you would like for each stage of labour, comfort measures you\220d like to have available, what monitoring or interventions you would like to choose or avoid. Make sure to include what you would like your midwives to do, whether you would prefer them in the background or if you would really like the reassurance of having them right next to you when they\220re in the room. Include how you would like baby to be born, whether you would like direction from a caregiver or not and if you would be happy to accept forceps etc if thought necessary.)/E(Next consider what you would like for each stage of labour, comfort measures you\220d like to have available, what monitoring or interventions you would like to choose or avoid. Make sure to include what you would like your midwives to do, whether you would prefer them in the background or if you would really like the reassurance of having them right next to you when they\220re in the room. Include how you would like baby to be born, whether you would like direction from a caregiver or not and if you would be happy to accept forceps etc if thought necessary.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

