439 0 obj
<</Title(Find out others experiences. For example, If you would love a home birth and you have gestational diabetes, Join a FB group like Home Birth Support Group UK and look for others experiences with GD. This can be a great way of getting some insight into what other people have found useful when making their decisions and the different care provider opinions others have come across. This might show you that it\220s not as black and white as you may have been led to believe. No matter what it is always your choice.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 435 0 R/Next 441 0 R>>
endobj

440 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Curtain lowered)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 442 0 R/Next 436 0 R>>
endobj

441 0 obj
<</Title(Talk through your options with knowledgable folks. Leanne or the AIMS helpline would be a good start, they can tell you what they know, any relevant research and help you come up with a list of questions for you to ask your care providers as well as stuff to read up on.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 439 0 R/Next 443 0 R>>
endobj

442 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Announce gender or not)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 444 0 R/Next 440 0 R>>
endobj

443 0 obj
<</Title(Discuss with your care provider. This may be a midwife or a consultant, do not be disheartened if you don\220t hear what you would like to hear, you can still chat through your circumstances with a Professional Midwifery Advocate and they can talk you through if what you are after is REALLY out of the question or not. \(note, it rarely is!\))/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 441 0 R/Next 445 0 R>>
endobj

444 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Gentle birth)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 446 0 R/Next 442 0 R>>
endobj

445 0 obj
<</Title(Consider what things are super important to you and you would not like to miss out on unless theres an emergency. This may be remaining upright throughout labour and for the birth, skin to skin after birth, avoiding \217the drip\220 or any other intervention or medication etc. How can you try to make sure that you can have these things? Can they be worked into all your birth plans? Eg. Remaining upright- even in the case of epidural use you can be assisted into various positions that support birth. Skin to skin after birth, can it be arranged that your birth partner holds baby on your chest for skin to skin EVEN after a Caesarean under general anaesthetic? Avoiding \217the drip\220, this may mean you opt for a caesarean if you would rather. There are so many possibilities we\220re not always offered, if you aren\220t sure how you can still incorporate certain things then talk to your instructor!)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 443 0 R/Next 447 0 R>>
endobj

446 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Breathing)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 448 0 R/Next 444 0 R>>
endobj

447 0 obj
<</Title(Create the birth plans for real! Consider everything you\220ve learned about any factors concerning your pregnancy and chats with PMA or midwife etc and bring it all together to create your plan using whichever format suits you best, try to ensure it will be easily read by the care providers and explained by your birth partner.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 445 0 R/Next 449 0 R>>
endobj

448 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Which hand for cannula)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 450 0 R/Next 446 0 R>>
endobj

449 0 obj
<</Title(Create your plan methodically by first considering your background such as how you feel about birth, how many babies you\220ve had, any special medical or cultural requirements.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 447 0 R/Next 451 0 R>>
endobj

450 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Where to place CTG)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 452 0 R/Next 448 0 R>>
endobj

451 0 obj
<</Title(Then move onto the things that you would like to include in your environment such as low light levels, quiet, who you would like present \(eg. Are you happy to have student midwives present? A doula?\).)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 449 0 R/Next 453 0 R>>
endobj

452 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Partner \(affirmations, touch, cuddles etc\))/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 454 0 R/Next 450 0 R>>
endobj

453 0 obj
<</Title(Next consider what you would like for each stage of labour, comfort measures you\220d like to have available, what monitoring or interventions you would like to choose or avoid. Make sure to include what you would like your midwives to do, whether you would prefer them in the background or if you would really like the reassurance of having them right next to you when they\220re in the room. Include how you would like baby to be born, whether you would like direction from a caregiver or not and if you would be happy to accept forceps etc if thought necessary.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 451 0 R/Next 455 0 R>>
endobj

454 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Music)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 456 0 R/Next 452 0 R>>
endobj

455 0 obj
<</Title(Then consider what you would like to happen once baby is here, would you like to find out the sex yourself?)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 453 0 R/Next 457 0 R>>
endobj

456 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Scripts)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 458 0 R/Next 454 0 R>>
endobj

457 0 obj
<</Title(Who will cut the cord? When will it be clamped \(if at all\)?)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 455 0 R/Next 459 0 R>>
endobj

458 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Lights)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 460 0 R/Next 456 0 R>>
endobj

459 0 obj
<</Title(What about vitamin K injection for baby? Let those reading know how you would like to feed your baby and what you would like to happen with baby when they are born, would you like uninterrupted skin to skin?)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 457 0 R/Next 461 0 R>>
endobj

460 0 obj
<</Title(\200 You have to agree and consent- how do you feel?)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 462 0 R/Next 458 0 R>>
endobj

461 0 obj
<</Title(Would you like baby wiped down before you hold them? This is all up to you! Finally, how would you like to birth the placenta? What would you like to do with it after?)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 459 0 R/Next 463 0 R>>
endobj

462 0 obj
<</Title(\200 Emergency vs unplanned)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 464 0 R/Next 460 0 R>>
endobj

463 0 obj
<</Title(Do this with your birth partner ideally so that they understand it all and know the reasons for your choices. At the very least, go through it in detail with them, they will then be able to help relay it to your care providers on the day.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 461 0 R/Next 465 0 R>>
endobj

464 0 obj
